// MsgResetAllocations clears every stake-weighted allocation vote, so the
// emission stream is only directed by stakers who show up and vote again.
//
// Votes are cast once and then persist indefinitely, so over time the split
// reflects whoever was active when they last voted rather than who is active
// now. This retires the whole slate at once.
//
// Options survive along with any ERTH they have already accrued, so no recipient
// loses a claimable balance and nobody re-pays the address-option fee. Staked
// balances are untouched. Until voters return, the stream simply accrues to
// nothing.
